From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:47:38 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: correct the CBM pool precondition

The precondition on the CBM buffer pools says the FRITZ!Box 7590 has 224
MiB. It has 512, and had 256 before that -- the number went stale twice
while the constraint it was illustrating never moved.

State it against the address instead. The pools end at 0x25200000, the
smallest memory node on the platform is the FRITZ!Box 7560's 128 MiB
ending at 0x28000000, and every board clears the pools by at least 46
MiB. That sentence stays true however much DRAM a future board carries,
which the old one could not.

Comment only; no DTB changes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi
index bdef191a7cdf..cea39f817ddf 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi
@@ -147,10 +147,11 @@ port@3 {
